        <mxCell id="n42" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n19" target="n20"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n43" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n18" target="n21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n44" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n21" target="n7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n45" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n7" target="n22"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n46" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n22" target="n25"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n47" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n22" target="n23"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n48" value="THERE IS NO REFRESH ENDPOINT&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The refresh token is signed at login and written to users.refresh_token, and&lt;br&gt;then nothing ever reads it. AuthController has login, register, OTP, firebase,&lt;br&gt;forgot-password, change-password, logout and profile — and no route that&lt;br&gt;exchanges a refresh token for a new access token.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;So the second half of the usual pair does not exist. When the access token&lt;br&gt;expires the user is simply logged out and types their password again. The&lt;br&gt;refresh token is a stored credential that buys nothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Worth stating plainly at the defence, because the diagram of a login flow&lt;br&gt;normally implies a refresh loop, and a grader will look for it. Either build&lt;br&gt;POST /auth/refresh, or stop issuing and storing the token.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Storing it is not free: user.entity.ts already notes that a leaked row hands&lt;br&gt;over a valid refresh token, and nothing checks whether the stored one matches&lt;br&gt;the one presented — because nothing presents one." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1290" width="820" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n49" value="What token_version buys, and what it costs&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A JWT cannot be withdrawn once handed out — that is the trade a stateless&lt;br&gt;token makes. token_version buys the withdrawal back: the number is signed into&lt;br&gt;the payload, JwtStrategy compares it against the row on EVERY request, and&lt;br&gt;logout increments it. Every token issued before that moment stops working at&lt;br&gt;once, on every device.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;That is the right call for a system holding money. A stolen token stops being&lt;br&gt;useful the moment the owner logs out, instead of staying valid until it&lt;br&gt;expires.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The cost is one row read per authenticated request, which is exactly the cost&lt;br&gt;a stateless token was supposed to avoid. Worth it here; worth knowing it is&lt;br&gt;the reason `users` is the hottest table in the system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The parallel bars are a real fork: the two tokens are signed independently and&lt;br&gt;the response needs both. UML requires the fork to be closed by a join, and&lt;br&gt;the join is what the response waits on." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="890" y="1290" width="820" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
